IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), PART VII.1, section 152.05: benefits for the care of a new-born or
-- adopted child (parental benefits) payable to a self-employed person.
-- Piece ei5, written by the piece agent ei5 (Sonnet 5.5). Layer 1: from the Act's text alone, no point of view.
--
-- The 35-week or 61-week maximum and its division are the keel's `Election of maximum weeks`. The weeks and the
-- maxima of s 152.14 (which this section keeps referring to) are in ei5-payment; here the figures the section states
-- itself (40, 69, 35, 61, 52, 104, 26, 50) are written out and cited.
-- The provincial-law reduction of subsection (11) is the shared rule in ei5-sickness-pregnancy
-- (`ss 152.03(2), 152.04(3), 152.05(11), ... benefits after the reduction prescribed ...`).
-- Dates: no enactment or commencement date in this section.

§ `152.05 Benefits -- parental benefits (care of a new-born or adopted child)`

-- src:2194 | 152.05 (1) Subject to this Part, benefits are payable to a self-employed person to care for one or more new-born children of the person or one or more children placed with the person for the purpose of adoption under the laws governing adoption in the province in which the person resides.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(1) (src:2194)
GIVEN `to care for one or more new-born children of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to care for one or more children placed with the person for the purpose of adoption under the laws governing adoption in the province in which the person resides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.05(1) benefits are payable for the care of a child` IF
       `to care for one or more new-born children of the person`
    OR `to care for one or more children placed with the person for the purpose of adoption under the laws governing adoption in the province in which the person resides`

-- Subsection (1.1): in a claim under this section the self-employed person "shall elect" the 35-week or the 61-week
-- maximum. A claim under this section that makes no election does not meet the requirement.
-- src:2196 | (1.1) In a claim for benefits made under this section, a self-employed person shall elect the maximum number of weeks referred to in either subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(i) or (ii) for which benefits may be paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(1.1) (src:2196)
GIVEN `the claim is made under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim elects the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(i) or (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.05(1.1) the claim meets the requirement to elect` IF
        NOT (`the claim is made under this section`)
    OR  `the claim elects the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(i) or (ii)`

-- src:2198 | (1.2) The election is irrevocable once benefits are paid under this section or under section 23 in respect of the same child or children.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(1.2) (src:2198)
GIVEN `benefits have been paid under this section in respect of the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits have been paid under section 23 in respect of the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 23 (piece ei1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.05(1.2) the election is irrevocable` IF
       `benefits have been paid under this section in respect of the same child or children`
    OR `benefits have been paid under section 23 in respect of the same child or children`

-- Subsection (1.3): where two persons claim for the same child or children (two self-employed persons, or one and a
-- person claiming under s 23), the election of the first to make a claim is binding on both. The other person's
-- election is NOTHING when they have not claimed.
-- src:2200 | (1.3) If two self-employed persons each make a claim for benefits under this section — or if one self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23 — in respect of the same child or children, the election made under subsection (1.1) or subsection 23(1.1) by the first person to make a claim for benefits under this section or under section 23 is binding on both persons.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(1.3) (src:2200)
GIVEN `the election I made` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `the election made by the other person who claims in respect of the same child or children` IS A MAYBE `Election of maximum weeks`
      `I was the first to make a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Election of maximum weeks`
DECIDE `s 152.05(1.3) the election that binds the person` IS
    CONSIDER `the election made by the other person who claims in respect of the same child or children`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the election I made`
    WHEN JUST other THEN IF `I was the first to make a claim` THEN `the election I made` ELSE other

§§ `152.05(2) to (7) The period for which parental benefits are payable`

-- Subsection (2): the period begins with the week in which the child is born or placed and ends 52 weeks after that
-- week. Read as whole weeks: it begins on the Sunday of that week and ends on the Saturday of the week 52 weeks
-- after it (fork F8).
-- src:2202 | (2) Subject to section 152.14, benefits under this section are payable for each week of unemployment in the period
-- src:2203 | (a) that begins with the week in which the child or children of the self-employed person are born or the child or children are actually placed with the self-employed person for the purpose of adoption; and
-- src:2204 | (b) that ends 52 weeks after the week in which the child or children of the self-employed person are born or the child or children are actually placed with the self-employed person for the purpose of adoption.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(2) (src:2202-2204)
GIVEN `the day on which the child or children are born or are actually placed for the purpose of adoption` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 152.05(2) the period for which parental benefits are payable` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the week of the birth or placement`,
                        `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (`the week of the birth or placement` PLUS (`weeks as days` 52))
    WHERE
        `the week of the birth or placement` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which the child or children are born or are actually placed for the purpose of adoption`

-- Subsections (3) and (4): if the child or children are hospitalized during the period, it is extended by the number of
-- weeks of hospitalization, but never to more than 104 weeks (a period of 104 whole weeks from its first day).
-- src:2206 | (3) If the child or children referred to in subsection (1) are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection (2), the period is extended by the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized.
-- src:2208 | (4) No extension under subsection (3) may result in the period being longer than 104 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(3) and (4) (src:2206) (src:2208)
GIVEN `the period referred to in subsection (2)` IS A `Period of days`
      `the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 152.05(3) and (4) the period extended because the child or children are hospitalized` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the period referred to in subsection (2)`'s `first day of the period`,
                        IF `the extended last day` LESS THAN `the longest permitted last day`
                        THEN `the extended last day`
                        ELSE `the longest permitted last day`
    WHERE
        `the extended last day` MEANS
            `the period referred to in subsection (2)`'s `last day of the period` PLUS (`weeks as days` `the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized`)
        `the longest permitted last day` MEANS
            `the period referred to in subsection (2)`'s `first day of the period` PLUS ((`weeks as days` 104) MINUS 1)

-- Subsection (5): during the benefit period benefits were paid for more than one of the reasons in paragraphs
-- 152.14(1)(a) to (f), the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons is greater than 50, and
-- benefits were paid for the reason in 152.14(1)(b) but for fewer than the applicable maximum (35 or 61) for it: the
-- period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to that maximum. The text does not say by how many calendar
-- weeks the period is extended, only that benefits may then be paid up to the maximum, so the rule gives the
-- condition and the number of weeks of benefits that may still be paid (see "what the source does not answer").
-- src:2210 | (5) If, during a self-employed person’s benefit period, benefits were paid to the person for more than one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f), the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons is greater than 50, and benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b) but for fewer than the applicable maximum number of weeks established for that reason, the period referred to in subsection (2) is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(i) or (ii).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(5) (src:2210)
GIVEN `the number of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f) for which benefits were paid during the benefit period` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks for which benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicable maximum number of weeks established for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.05(5) the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum` IF
        `the number of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f) for which benefits were paid during the benefit period` GREATER THAN 1
    AND `the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons` GREATER THAN 50
    AND `the number of weeks for which benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the number of weeks for which benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)` LESS THAN `the applicable maximum number of weeks established for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)`

-- src:2210 | (5) If, during a self-employed person’s benefit period, benefits were paid to the person for more than one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f), the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons is greater than 50, and benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b) but for fewer than the applicable maximum number of weeks established for that reason, the period referred to in subsection (2) is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(i) or (ii).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(5) (src:2210)
GIVEN `the period is extended under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks for which benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicable maximum number of weeks established for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.05(5) the number of weeks of benefits that may be paid, up to the applicable maximum, after the extension` IS
    IF `the period is extended under subsection (5)`
    THEN `the applicable maximum number of weeks established for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)` MINUS `the number of weeks for which benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)`
    ELSE 0

-- Subsection (5.1): no benefits were paid for any reason in 152.14(1)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f), and benefits were paid
-- for the reason in 152.14(1)(b) where the applicable maximum is the 61 weeks of subparagraph (b)(ii): the period is
-- extended by 26 weeks.
-- src:2212 | (5.1) If, during a self-employed person’s benefit period, benefits were not paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f) and benefits were paid to the person for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b) in the case where the applicable maximum number of weeks is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(ii), the period referred to in subsection (2) is extended by 26 weeks so that benefits may be paid up to that maximum number of weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(5.1) (src:2212)
GIVEN `benefits were paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election made` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.05(5.1) the number of weeks by which the period is extended` IS
    IF     NOT (`benefits were paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f)`)
       AND `benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)`
       AND `the election made` EQUALS `the 61-week maximum`
    THEN 26
    ELSE 0

-- Subsection (6): the extension under (5) must not make the period longer than the maximum benefit period calculated
-- under subsection 152.11(16) (ei5-benefit-period computes it; a caller passes it).
-- src:2214 | (6) An extension under subsection (5) must not result in the period referred to in subsection (2) being longer than the maximum benefit period calculated under subsection 152.11(16).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(6) (src:2214)
GIVEN `the length of the period in weeks after the extension under subsection (5)` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum benefit period calculated under subsection 152.11(16), in weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.05(6) the length of the period after an extension under subsection (5)` IS
    min `the length of the period in weeks after the extension under subsection (5)` `the maximum benefit period calculated under subsection 152.11(16), in weeks`

-- Subsection (7): an extension under one or more of subsections 152.11(11) to (14.1) must not make the period longer
-- than 104 weeks.
-- src:2216 | (7) An extension under one or more of subsections 152.11(11) to (14.1) must not result in the period referred to in subsection (2) being longer than 104 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(7) (src:2216)
GIVEN `the length of the period in weeks after the extension under subsections 152.11(11) to (14.1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.05(7) the length of the period after an extension under subsections 152.11(11) to (14.1)` IS
    min `the length of the period in weeks after the extension under subsections 152.11(11) to (14.1)` 104

§§ `152.05(12) to (15) Division of the weeks, and the waiting period`

-- Subsections (12) and (13): where two persons claim for the same child or children, the weeks payable under this
-- section, under section 23 or under both may be divided between them up to 40 weeks if the election is the 35-week
-- maximum and up to 69 weeks if it is the 61-week maximum.
-- src:2221 | (12) If two self-employed persons each make a claim for benefits under this section — or if one self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23 — in respect of the same child or children, the weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23 or under both those sections may be divided between them up to a maximum of 40, if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection (1.1) or 23(1.1) is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(i) or 12(3)(b)(i), or up to a maximum of 69, if that number of weeks is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(ii) or 12(3)(b)(ii). If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:2223 | (13) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same child or children, a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 23 that may be divided between them may not exceed
-- src:2224 | (a) 40, if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection (1.1) or 23(1.1) is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(i) or 12(3)(b)(i); or
-- src:2225 | (b) 69, if that number of weeks is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(ii) or 12(3)(b)(ii).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(12) and (13) (src:2221) (src:2223-2225)
GIVEN `the election made` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ss 152.05(12) and (13) the maximum number of weeks of benefits that may be divided between two claimants` IS
    CONSIDER `the election made`
    WHEN `the 35-week maximum` THEN 40
    WHEN `the 61-week maximum` THEN 69

-- Subsection (13.01): even if divided, no claimant is paid for more than 35 or 61 weeks, by the election.
-- src:2227 | (13.01) Even if the weeks of benefits payable are divided in accordance with subsections (12) and (13), the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to a claimant is 35 or 61 weeks, in accordance with the election made under subsection (1.1) or 23(1.1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(13.01) (src:2227)
GIVEN `the election made` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.05(13.01) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to a claimant` IS
    CONSIDER `the election made`
    WHEN `the 35-week maximum` THEN 35
    WHEN `the 61-week maximum` THEN 61

-- A proposed division is within the limits when the two shares together do not exceed (12)/(13) and neither share
-- exceeds (13.01).
-- src:2221 | (12) If two self-employed persons each make a claim for benefits under this section — or if one self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23 — in respect of the same child or children, the weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23 or under both those sections may be divided between them up to a maximum of 40, if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection (1.1) or 23(1.1) is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(i) or 12(3)(b)(i), or up to a maximum of 69, if that number of weeks is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(ii) or 12(3)(b)(ii). If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:2223 | (13) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same child or children, a self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 23 that may be divided between them may not exceed
-- src:2224 | (a) 40, if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection (1.1) or 23(1.1) is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(i) or 12(3)(b)(i); or
-- src:2225 | (b) 69, if that number of weeks is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(ii) or 12(3)(b)(ii).
-- src:2226 | Maximum number of weeks per claimant
-- src:2227 | (13.01) Even if the weeks of benefits payable are divided in accordance with subsections (12) and (13), the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to a claimant is 35 or 61 weeks, in accordance with the election made under subsection (1.1) or 23(1.1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(12), (13) and (13.01) (src:2221) (src:2223-2227)
GIVEN `the election made` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `the weeks of benefits to one of the two claimants` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits to the other claimant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.05(12), (13) and (13.01) a division of the weeks of benefits is within the limits` IF
        `the weeks of benefits to one of the two claimants` PLUS `the weeks of benefits to the other claimant`
            AT MOST `ss 152.05(12) and (13) the maximum number of weeks of benefits that may be divided between two claimants` `the election made`
    AND `the weeks of benefits to one of the two claimants` AT MOST `s 152.05(13.01) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to a claimant` `the election made`
    AND `the weeks of benefits to the other claimant` AT MOST `s 152.05(13.01) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to a claimant` `the election made`

-- Subsection (12), last sentence: the claimants divide the weeks in the manner they agree; if they cannot agree the
-- weeks are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules (reg 41.6, piece er3).
-- src:2221 | (12) If two self-employed persons each make a claim for benefits under this section — or if one self-employed person makes a claim for benefits under this section and another person makes a claim for benefits under section 23 — in respect of the same child or children, the weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 23 or under both those sections may be divided between them up to a maximum of 40, if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection (1.1) or 23(1.1) is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(i) or 12(3)(b)(i), or up to a maximum of 69, if that number of weeks is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(ii) or 12(3)(b)(ii). If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(12) (src:2221)
GIVEN `the two claimants agree on a division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weeks I am to receive under the division they agreed` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks I am to receive under the prescribed rules` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: reg 41.6 (piece er3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.05(12) the weeks of benefits to be paid to a claimant after the division` IS
    IF `the two claimants agree on a division`
    THEN `the weeks I am to receive under the division they agreed`
    ELSE `the weeks I am to receive under the prescribed rules`

-- Subsection (14): the waiting period may be deferred, to another claim in the same benefit period (not under s 152.04
-- or this section), in any of four cases.
-- src:2229 | (14) A self-employed person who makes a claim for benefits under this section may have his or her waiting period deferred until he or she makes another claim for benefits in the same benefit period, otherwise than under section 152.04 or this section, if
-- src:2230 | (a) the self-employed person has already made a claim for benefits under section 152.04 or this section in respect of the same child or children and has served the waiting period;
-- src:2231 | (b) another self-employed person has made a claim for benefits under section 152.04 or this section in respect of the same child or children and that other self-employed person has served or is serving his or her waiting period;
-- src:2232 | (c) another self-employed person is making a claim for benefits under section 152.04 or this section in respect of the same child or children at the same time as the self-employed person and that other self-employed person elects to serve the waiting period; or
-- src:2233 | (d) the self-employed person or another self-employed person meets the prescribed requirements.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(14) (src:2229-2233)
GIVEN `the person has already made a claim for benefits under section 152.04 or this section in respect of the same child or children and has served the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another self-employed person has made a claim under section 152.04 or this section in respect of the same child or children and has served or is serving their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another self-employed person is making such a claim at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or another self-employed person meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 152.05(14)(d); no such regulation found (pieces er1 to er6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.05(14) the waiting period may be deferred` IF
       `the person has already made a claim for benefits under section 152.04 or this section in respect of the same child or children and has served the waiting period`
    OR `another self-employed person has made a claim under section 152.04 or this section in respect of the same child or children and has served or is serving their waiting period`
    OR `another self-employed person is making such a claim at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period`
    OR `the person or another self-employed person meets the prescribed requirements`

-- Subsection (15): a self-employed person claims under this Part and another person claims under s 22 or 23 for the
-- same child or children, and one of them has served or elected to serve their waiting period: (a) the self-employed
-- person, if not the one who served or elected, need not serve a waiting period; (b) the other person, if not the one
-- who served or elected, may have their waiting period deferred under s 23.
-- src:2235 | (15) If a self-employed person makes a claim under this Part and another person makes a claim under section 22 or 23 in respect of the same child or children and one of them has served or elected to serve their waiting period, then
-- src:2236 | (a) if the self-employed person is not the one who served or elected to serve the waiting period, the self-employed person is not required to serve a waiting period; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(15)(a) (src:2235-2236)
GIVEN `another person makes a claim under section 22 or 23 in respect of the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of them has served or elected to serve their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the self-employed person is the one who served or elected to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.05(15)(a) the self-employed person is not required to serve a waiting period` IF
        `another person makes a claim under section 22 or 23 in respect of the same child or children`
    AND `one of them has served or elected to serve their waiting period`
    AND NOT (`the self-employed person is the one who served or elected to serve the waiting period`)

-- src:2235 | (15) If a self-employed person makes a claim under this Part and another person makes a claim under section 22 or 23 in respect of the same child or children and one of them has served or elected to serve their waiting period, then
-- src:2237 | (b) if the person making the claim under section 22 or 23 is not the one who served or elected to serve the waiting period, the person may have his or her waiting period deferred in accordance with section 23.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.05(15)(b) (src:2235) (src:2237)
GIVEN `another person makes a claim under section 22 or 23 in respect of the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of them has served or elected to serve their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making the claim under section 22 or 23 is the one who served or elected to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.05(15)(b) the person making the claim under section 22 or 23 may have their waiting period deferred in accordance with section 23` IF
        `another person makes a claim under section 22 or 23 in respect of the same child or children`
    AND `one of them has served or elected to serve their waiting period`
    AND NOT (`the person making the claim under section 22 or 23 is the one who served or elected to serve the waiting period`)
